    "durationMs": 247963,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL Shortener API is complete in `/workspace`, built with ASP.NET Core 8.0 (net8.0, runtime 8.0.15) minimal APIs and EF Core 8 + Npgsql as the persistence layer.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `Program.cs` — minimal API endpoints: `POST /links` (201 with `{code, url, clicks: 0}`, generated or custom codes), `GET /links` (ascending by creation id, `{items, total}`), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), `GET /r/{code}` (302 with `Location` = stored URL, atomic `ExecuteUpdate` click increment). Bodies are parsed explicitly so malformed JSON returns 422 with an `error` field instead of the framework's default 400.\n- Validation — URL must be an absolute http/https URI with a host; codes must match `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`; violations, missing url, malformed JSON, and non-string fields all return 422; duplicate custom codes return 409 (pre-check plus unique-index catch for races).\n- Persistence — `Links` table with unique code index, EF migration in `Migrations/`, applied at startup via `MigrateAsync`; `ConnectionStrings.cs` parses the `DATABASE_URL` PostgreSQL URL into an Npgsql connection string (nothing hard-coded).\n- `start.sh` — applies migrations then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`, with a rebuild fallback if `publish/` is missing. README documents startup.\n\n**Verified** (42-check curl suite + boundary tests): all status codes and body shapes exact, URL returned unchanged, 4/20-char code boundaries, duplicate → 409, every 422 case, redirect Location header byte-exact, clicks incremented exactly once per redirect, and full state (data + click counts) survived a kill/restart cycle. The server is stopped, so port 8000 is free for the graded `sh start.sh` run."
